|passage=“Clinton,” Gail cried from outside, “are you going to sit on the '''pot''' all day?”}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=27 December 2011|author=Ken Jacuzzi|coauthors=Diane Holloway|chapter=This Is Your Life, Ken Jacuzzi!|title=Jacuzzi: A Father’s Invention to Ease a Son’s Pain|location=Bloomington, Ind.|publisher=w:iUniverse|section=part III (Learning, Marriage, and Stuff)|page=385|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=GzgEN5PAOnYC&pg=PA385|isbn=978-0-595-37097-9|passage=Near bedtime, about 10 p.m. or so, I sit on the '''pot'''. My “routine” is at night so as to shorten the morning get readies and start work on time. Sometimes the p.m. '''pot''' routine is successful, sometimes not. I can only blame myself, of course, when the big event doesn’t occur. I need to drink more water during the day.}}
