#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Trollerʻs Guide: A New and Complete Practical Treatise on the Art of Trolling Or Fishing for Jack and Pike|year=1820|author=Thomas Frederick Salter|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=jS8CAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22pouched%20the%22&pg=PA51#v=onepage&q=%22pouched%20the%22&f=false|passage={{...}} but if they shake the line and move, after they have remained still three or four minutes, you may conclude the fish has '''pouched''' the bait and feels the hooks, then wind up your slack and strike, but not violently, and always mind to keep the point of your rod a little raised while you are playing and killing your fish {{...}}}}
