===Etymology 2===
Ellipsis of {{m|en||I pray you}}, {{m|en||I pray thee}}, whence also {{m|en|prithee}}.

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|archaic|or|formal}} [[please|Please]]; {{n-g|used to make a polite [[request]]}}
#: {{ux|en|'''pray''' silence for…}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Emma|volume=I|page=124|text="'''Pray''', Mr. Knightley," said Emma, who had been smiling to herself through a great part of this speech, "how do you know that Mr. Martin did not speak yesterday?"}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Old Curiosity Shop|chapter=10|page=144|text='''Pray''' don’t ask me why, '''pray''' don’t be sorry, '''pray''' don’t be vexed with me, I have nothing to do with it indeed!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1845|author=w:Frederick Marryat|title=s:The Mission|chapter=[[s:The Mission/Chapter XXI|Chapter XXI]]|text=''Well, Major, '''pray''' tell us your adventures, for you have frightened us dreadfully.''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|author=w:Arthur Conan Doyle|title=s:The Adventure of the Engineer's Thumb|text=Thank you. I am sorry to have interrupted you. '''Pray''' continue your most interesting statement.}}
# {{alternative form of|en|pray tell||I ask you}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1981|author=w:A. D. Hope|chapter=His Coy Mistress to Mr. Marvell|chapterurl=https://allpoetry.com/His-Coy-Mistress-To-Mr.-Marvell|title=A Book of Answers
|passage=Shall I be moved to love you, '''pray,''' / By hints that I must soon decay? / No woman's won by being told / How quickly she is growing old[...]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=20 September 2013|author=Martina Hyde|title=Is the pope Catholic?|journal=The Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/sep/20/is-pope-catholic-atheists-gay-people-abortion|text=He is a South American, so perhaps revolutionary spirit courses through Francis's veins. But what, '''pray''', does the Catholic church want with doubt?}}

