===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*plew-|*plewk-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|plumage}}, {{m|enm|plummage|t=bird’s feathers collectively, plumage; (''falconry'') feathers fed to a hawk to cause it to regurgitate, casting}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=plumāǧe|pos=n|id=MED33782}}</ref> from {{der|en|frm|plumage}}, {{m|frm|plomage|t=bird’s feathers collectively; person’s (showy) clothing}}, from {{der|en|fro|plumage|t=bird’s feathers collectively}} (modern {{cog|fr|plumage}}), from {{m|fro|plume|t=feather, plume}} + {{m|fro|-age|pos={{lg|suffix}} forming {{lg|noun}}s denoting a state of being}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=7243685039|date=March 2026|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> {{m|fro||Plume}} is derived from {{der|en|la|plūma|t=feather, plume}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*plewk-|t=to flow; to fly; to run; etc.}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*plew-|t=to flow; to fly; to run}}. {{surf|en|plume|-age|pos2=suffix forming nouns with a sense of appurtenance or collection}}.

